I have completed the exploratory data analysis on the Circana Neutrogena Sun Care (2022–2026, 196 DMAs) dataset. Below is a concise summary of the key findings, our proposed DMA grouping framework, and recommendations for sign-off before we bring in the media datasets.
1. Key Findings from Sales EDA
Brand Sizing & Category Share (Charts 1–2):
Ultra Sheer ($727.5M, 41.8%) and Beach Defense ($460.8M, 26.5%) together drive ~68% of all Neutrogena Sun sales, followed by Clear Face (9.7%) and Sport (6.2%).
Total Sun category avg weekly sales grew ~40% ($33.9M/wk in 2022 to $47.3M/wk in 2026 YTD [45 weeks]), while NTG grew slower ($5.9M/wk to $7.7M/wk). As a result, NTG’s category share peaked at 19.0% in 2023 and declined to 16.2% in 2026, while Ultra Sheer held steady at 41%–43% of NTG.
Seasonality: "Everyday" Ultra Sheer vs. "Seasonal" Beach Defense (Charts 3–6):
Ultra Sheer moves almost 1:1 with Total NTG Sun (0.99 weekly correlation; 0.95 with Beach Defense) and shows a steadier ~9× peak-to-trough swing (12.7% winter share, 25.8% spring/fall shoulder share).
Beach Defense is heavily summer-concentrated (~24× swing): 71.5% of its annual sales occur in May–Aug (peaking at 3.67× around July 4th) and only 7.4% in Nov–Feb. Notably, Beach Defense’s peak-week sales nearly doubled from ~$4.2M/wk (2022) to ~$8.0M/wk (2025–2026).
Inside NTG, Ultra Sheer carries 44%–46% of sales in winter vs. 15%–18% for Beach Defense; by July 4th (Weeks 26–27), Beach Defense surges to 36.2%—nearly matching Ultra Sheer (36.7%).
DMA Concentration & Geographic Footprint (Charts 7–8):
Sales are highly concentrated: Top 18 DMAs = 50%, Top 60 DMAs = 80.3% (≥ $26.7K/wk), and Top 100 DMAs = 91.3% (≥ $13.6K/wk). The bottom 96 Tail DMAs (#101–196) contribute only 8.7% of sales (dropping down to $558/wk in Alpena, MI).
